"""An MCP server over Goanna's control channel (docs/control-channel.md).

The channel is the interface and this is a wrapper over it, so everything
here can be done from a shell with tools/goanna-control. What the wrapper
adds is the session: starting clients, rebuilding and relaunching them after
a C++ change, and handing back a shot already checked by shotcheck.

Clients are instances. goanna_session start runs one from any checkout or
worktree, headless by default (tools/goanna_headless.py: inside gamescope's
headless backend, so no window, focus change or pointer grab reaches the
desktop), and returns an instance id that every other tool takes. Several
can run at once, each on its own control port, and every reply says which
instance and port it acted on. start_vanilla runs the vanilla Luanti client
the same way, for reference frames.

It speaks MCP over stdin and stdout, as newline delimited JSON-RPC, with no
dependencies beyond the standard library. Register it with:

    claude mcp add goanna /path/to/goanna/tools/goanna-mcp

Nothing may print to stdout except protocol messages. Diagnostics go to
stderr, and the clients' own output goes to log files.
"""

